! ===========================================================================
! samsung-tv-account-voice.blocklist
! OPT-IN LAYER - not applied by default.
!
! Apply this ON TOP OF samsung-tv-telemetry.blocklist, and only after you have
! decided to give up the Samsung account and/or voice control.
!
! What this layer costs you:
!   * Samsung account sign-in breaks entirely (you will not be able to sign
!     back in without removing this layer first)
!   * Bixby / voice control stops working
!   * Tizen Store purchase and login stop working
!
! What it gains you:
!   * no account-linked identity
!   * no viewing-history profile and no personalised recommendations
!   * no voice transcripts stored against an identity
!
! Why voice telemetry has no hostname of its own:
!   voice commands are transmitted to a third-party speech-recognition
!   provider together with device identifiers. The voice path shares
!   infrastructure with the account and wake-word services, so it cannot be
!   blocked at the DNS layer without breaking voice.
!   The reliable way to stop audio leaving the house is the device switch:
!     Settings -> General -> Voice Recognition -> Voice Assistant: Off
!
! Confirm every entry against your own query log before relying on it.
! ===========================================================================

! --- Account / SSO backend (breaks sign-in) ---
||auth.samsungosp.com^
||sc-auth.samsungosp.com^
||eu-auth2.samsungosp.com^
||account.samsung.com^
||samsungosp.com^

! --- Bixby voice assistant service (breaks voice) ---
||provisioning-use2.mgmt.aibixby.com^
||mgmt.aibixby.com^
||bixby.samsung.com^

! --- SmartThings account cloud (breaks pairing and account) ---
||samsungiotcloud.com^
